=== 0. Method, copies and the one thing the lead could not do

The repo was not edited. Every Rust run used a copy made with
  git -c core.autocrlf=false archive HEAD mathd | tar -x
in C:/Users/surya/AppData/Local/Temp/b5fb/. Content identity, HEAD vs copy
(`diff <(git show HEAD:mathd/<f>) <copy>/<f> | wc -l`, all 0):

  mathd/src/verifier.rs       content-diff-lines=0
  mathd/tests/verifier.rs     content-diff-lines=0
  mathd/fixtures/generate.py  content-diff-lines=0
  mathd/fixtures/verifier.json content-diff-lines=0

(the working tree has CRLF on this host, core.autocrlf=true, so byte hashes of
the two differ for the .rs/.py files while their content does not; the three
fixture JSONs have 0 CR bytes and match byte for byte).

cargo test cannot link on this host (no MSVC or mingw linker; a Git Bash
`/usr/bin/link` shadows the real one). The lead ported tests/verifier.rs to a
wasm cdylib with a rewriting script. That rewriting is what I wanted to avoid,
so this time the *unmodified* test binary was built for wasm32-wasip1 and run
under node:wasi:

  rustup target add wasm32-wasip1          (std for the target only)
  CARGO_TARGET_WASM32_WASIP1_RUNNER="node <abs>/wasi.mjs" \
  FB_PREOPEN="<copy of mathd, backslash path>" \
  cargo test --target wasm32-wasip1

wasi.mjs, in full (14 lines):
  import { WASI } from 'node:wasi';
  import { argv, env, cwd } from 'node:process';
  import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
  import { resolve } from 'node:path';
  const wasmPath = argv[2];
  const args = argv.slice(2);
  const preopens = { '.': '.' };
  // std's fs uses env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR") in some tests; expose it as a
  // guest-visible directory so those reads work under WASI.
  if (env.FB_PREOPEN) {
    for (const p of env.FB_PREOPEN.split(';')) if (p) preopens[p] = resolve(p);
  }
  const wasi = new WASI({ version: 'preview1', args, env: {}, preopens, returnOnExit: true });
  const mod = await WebAssembly.compile(readFileSync(wasmPath));
  const inst = await WebAssembly.instantiate(mod, wasi.getImportObject());
  const code = wasi.start(inst);
  process.exit(code ?? 0);

The second preopen exists because differentiator.rs and evaluator.rs build
paths from env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR"), which on this host is a Windows path
("C:\Users\...\src\mathd/fixtures/diff.json"); without it those two suites
panic on fs::read and the run says nothing about the code. With it they pass.
No test source was changed: the compiled bytes are the committed test file.

Toolchain: rustc 1.98.1, cargo 1.98.1, node v24.19.0, SymPy 1.14.0, mpmath
1.3.0, HEAD 0f19904.

