=== 10. Findings

V7 (BLOCKING, code): evidence reports points it never tested.
mathd/src/verifier.rs:197 returns
    Verdict::Verified { evidence: Evidence { points_tested: MIN_TEST_POINTS, ... } }
from the no-variables branch: the branch opens at line 177 and evaluates exactly
one point at line 179, once per side.
Before 396e319 this line read `points_tested: 1` and was true. The commit
changed it to 8 and did not mention it in its message (the message lists V1,
V2, V3, V5, V6). This is AGENTS.md rule 10 in its exact form ("Report counts
that match reality"), and `Evidence` is the field the card store will keep as
the proof of a Verified. Nothing in the suite notices either direction: F7
(reporting the honest 1) also passes, and no fixture case is a constant claim
(0 of 79 identity cases have an empty vars list).
Correct fix, either:
  (a) report 1 and say in a comment that a claim with no free variables is
      decided by one point (no variables, so one point is exhaustive); or
  (b) return Unverifiable with a reason naming the missing point count.
What is not acceptable is printing a threshold as if it were a measurement.
Add a test that pins the field: count the evaluations and assert
evidence.points_tested equals the count, for both the variable path (16) and
the constant path (1 or Unverifiable). That also kills break F2.

G1 (BLOCKING under the board's break rule, test): the evidence count is
unpinned. Break F2 (report points_tested + 8) passes all five verifier tests.
The board's rule is explicit that a suite which passes with a deliberate break
is a FAIL; here the break is a lie about the evidence, the same lie V7
introduced.

G2 (BLOCKING under the board's break rule, test): the V6 equation-parameter fix
is unpinned, and removing it reintroduces a false Verified. Break F5 (all
parameter regions positive) passes all five tests, and probe F shows
`abs(p) * x - p = 0`, claimed root [1], coming back as Verified under it. The
work order calls a false Verified project-stopping. Add probe F as a test that
must return Failed (the same shape as the author's own
test_verifier_rejects_negative_domain_false_claims, one level up: negative
parameters rather than negative x).

G3 (non-blocking): tests/verifier.rs:799 asserts true_negatives >= 1000 while
the real count is 2242. A regression that throws away 1,242 rejections (55% of
the mutation coverage) still passes. Pin the exact count, or a 1% band
(>= 2219), now that V6 makes the count stable and the fixture regenerates byte
for byte.

G4 (cosmetic): the FP and FN lines print "(actual false Verified count)" and
"(actual false rejection count)" next to the number. The lead asked for
computed rates or no rate; TP and TN now have rates, FP and FN have a label
that only restates the count. Either print the rate or drop the parenthetical.

Not a finding, recorded because it is easy to misread: the three fixture JSONs
have no CR bytes while the .rs/.py sources in the working tree are CRLF
(core.autocrlf=true). Regeneration is byte-identical to the committed JSONs, so
the line-ending setting does not reach the fixtures.

